WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.259 --> 00:00:01.830
(crowd cheering)

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:03.233
- [Announcer] And it's a good shot.

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:07.980
- We found something in our reporting,

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.790
something happening here in
the one big city in Qatar,

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:14.481
a place the whole world
is looking at right now,

00:00:14.481 --> 00:00:15.870
(dramatic music)

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:19.830
an invisible border drawn
to trap human beings,

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.650
to make them work, to make them build.

00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.450
I wanna show this to you.

00:00:24.450 --> 00:00:27.240
So, let me take you back
to show you how we ended up

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:28.770
sending a camera to someone

00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:31.230
and teaching them how to
shoot undercover in Qatar

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:34.650
while simultaneously capturing
interviews in rural Nepal

00:00:34.650 --> 00:00:37.410
and how I ended up here staring for hours

00:00:37.410 --> 00:00:39.990
at maps drawn by the Qatari government,

00:00:39.990 --> 00:00:42.330
all of this to shine a light on something

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:45.420
that Qatar doesn't want the world to see.

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.153
- [Raj] All of these have
been emptied very recently.

00:00:49.169 --> 00:00:50.002
(fingers tapping)

00:00:50.002 --> 00:00:51.780
(mouse clicking)

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:53.550
- Hey, I need to show you something.

00:00:53.550 --> 00:00:56.190
I've been looking at maps of Qatar

00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.900
because the World Cup is going there.

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.180
When the world is gonna
be fixated on one place,

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:01.260
you gotta look at all the maps.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:02.790
I've been on the
government website of Qatar

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.500
looking at their zoning maps.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.500
This is the city of Doha,
the capital of Qatar,

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.270
but look at this.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:11.310
The whole city is yellow,

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:14.370
and there's this one little shape of blue,

00:01:14.370 --> 00:01:15.840
Doha Industrial Area.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.400
I know we're talking about zoning.

00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:18.630
I think something's up here.

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:19.860
I've been trying to map this, like,

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:22.140
throw it on, like, my
other tools to map it

00:01:22.140 --> 00:01:24.060
and see if there's,
like, what this could be,

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:26.190
and it's not totally making sense.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.050
It's kind of cut off from
the rest of the city.

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:31.200
There's another municipality
kind of in between it and Doha,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.340
but it's a part of Doha.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.560
Usually, when you have
weird zoning like this,

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:35.760
there's something going on.

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.523
Since Qatar got awarded
the World Cup in 2010,

00:01:37.523 --> 00:01:39.390
there's been all sorts of issues

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:40.977
with their labor
conditions and all of that,

00:01:40.977 --> 00:01:42.720
and I think this has to do with that,

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:44.310
but I don't totally know.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.010
The World Cup is happening in a few weeks.

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:48.145
I wanna go to this place.

00:01:48.145 --> 00:01:48.978
(camera clicking)

00:01:48.978 --> 00:01:51.510
I need to reach out to Cammy,
one of our research producers.

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:52.440
We're gonna dive into this.

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:53.610
We're gonna figure it out.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.970
We're going to Doha, folks.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:59.520
Hey Cammy, I wanna go to
Qatar before the World Cup

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.140
to look at this one part of the city

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:02.670
that's completely zoned differently.

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:04.631
I think it has to do with,
like, the labor situation there.

00:02:04.631 --> 00:02:05.464
(printer beeping)

00:02:05.464 --> 00:02:06.748
I can't not print it.

00:02:06.748 --> 00:02:07.581
(paper rustling)

00:02:07.581 --> 00:02:10.020
All right, I'm going there.

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:12.240
We have to find a fixer, a local producer,

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.060
someone on the ground who
can help us not get arrested.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:16.700
I will follow up tomorrow
with more details.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:17.850
Doo, doo, doo, doo, doo, doo, doo.

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:18.948
- Hey.
- Going to Qatar.

00:02:18.948 --> 00:02:20.400
♪ Doong, doong, doong, doong,
doong, doong, doong, doong ♪

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:21.750
- Johnny, yes, let's do it.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:23.460
This sounds like a really great story,

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:25.020
and I'll happily go to Doha with you.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:27.630
I'll start researching right now.

00:02:27.630 --> 00:02:29.280
- I'm going to Qatar.

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.120
- Congratulations.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:33.543
I just want you to be smart.

00:02:34.534 --> 00:02:37.320
- I've been doing some
research, and I don't know

00:02:37.320 --> 00:02:40.110
how easy it's gonna be
for us to film places,

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.300
especially in the Industrial Area.

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.460
From what I've read, they're notoriously

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:46.950
not very kind to journalists.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:48.990
- The best part about the
Gulf is that these cities are,

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.760
like, so, like, cartoonish.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.070
This is a hotel in freaking Doha.

00:02:53.070 --> 00:02:53.903
Look at this.

00:02:53.903 --> 00:02:55.380
Opening later this year.

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:57.240
Can I stay in this hotel

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:59.580
that looks like a freaking half pipe?

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:00.870
I've always wanted to do this.

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.914
I've never had an excuse.

00:03:01.914 --> 00:03:04.590
(energetic music)

00:03:04.590 --> 00:03:07.320
- Doha fixer number one
referred me to someone else,

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:08.460
so fingers crossed

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.010
that Doha fixer number
two is gonna work out.

00:03:11.010 --> 00:03:12.180
- Drones, yes.

00:03:12.180 --> 00:03:14.888
Do you think they'll let
me fly my drone in Doha?

00:03:14.888 --> 00:03:15.990
- No.

00:03:15.990 --> 00:03:16.823
- [Johnny] Why?

00:03:16.823 --> 00:03:19.590
- NATO countries are helping
out doing anti-drone stuff

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:20.910
'cause they're afraid of, you know,

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:22.701
terrorist drones coming in so that, like-

00:03:22.701 --> 00:03:24.840
- [Johnny] Wait, but what
about just my DJI drone?

00:03:24.840 --> 00:03:27.030
- They're sending out anti-drones-

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:27.863
- [Johnny] Geez.

00:03:27.863 --> 00:03:28.696
- to net them.
(camera clicking)

00:03:28.696 --> 00:03:29.529
- [Johnny] Wait, what?

00:03:29.529 --> 00:03:30.510
- Yeah, oh, lemme show you.

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.210
- Okay, not great news, our
fixer hasn't found anybody

00:03:33.210 --> 00:03:35.310
in the Industrial Area
who wants to talk with us.

00:03:35.310 --> 00:03:37.950
It's not looking likely that
they're going to find anybody.

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:41.220
I'm gonna keep trying to connect
with anyone on the ground.

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:42.570
- I think it's a hiding people thing.

00:03:42.570 --> 00:03:44.340
I don't know, but I'm
trying to find a fixer

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:45.540
to help me get in there.

00:03:45.540 --> 00:03:46.470
- You're gonna go in there?

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:47.730
- Yes.

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.170
I mean it's just, it's not,
like, some secret part-

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.580
- You're supposed to be leaving in a week,

00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:52.830
and we haven't found any fixers.

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:55.290
We haven't found any people on
the ground who could help us.

00:03:55.290 --> 00:03:58.351
I'm just a bit concerned
of our timeline right now.

00:03:58.351 --> 00:04:01.018
(pensive music)

00:04:02.670 --> 00:04:05.190
- I think we found someone, a fixer

00:04:05.190 --> 00:04:09.150
who is deeply connected with
the worker population in Doha

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.040
and is potentially gonna help us

00:04:11.040 --> 00:04:12.600
to get into the Industrial Area.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:13.530
We're meeting with him

00:04:13.530 --> 00:04:14.910
on a call in a few minutes.
(app ringing)

00:04:14.910 --> 00:04:16.110
Here we go.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:16.943
Nice to meet you.

00:04:16.943 --> 00:04:17.776
How are you doing?

00:04:17.776 --> 00:04:20.670
- [Fixer] Fine, let's switch off the A/C.

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.280
- Did you get the proposal that
we sent over of what we're-

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:24.840
- [Fixer] Yeah, proposal, I read.

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:27.630
- We're not trying to get
any secretive footage.

00:04:27.630 --> 00:04:30.930
It's more just about life
in the Industrial Area.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.640
I guess my question for you is, like,

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.490
if I went into the Industrial
Area with my camera,

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:38.422
not a big crew but just
my camera to go film-

00:04:38.422 --> 00:04:39.255
- [Fixer] What camera?

00:04:39.255 --> 00:04:40.088
- Like this.

00:04:40.088 --> 00:04:42.840
If I went into the Industrial
Area with this camera-

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:43.673
- [Fixer] No, no, no.

00:04:43.673 --> 00:04:44.610
- and filmed
- [Fixer] No.

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:48.030
Another thing, your skin color
is also a problem, you know?

00:04:48.030 --> 00:04:49.440
- Ah, explain that.

00:04:49.440 --> 00:04:50.273
What do you mean?

00:04:50.273 --> 00:04:52.276
- [Fixer] Yeah, it will make, you know,

00:04:52.276 --> 00:04:54.060
you will get undue attention.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.664
- From who do you think I
would get undue attention?

00:04:56.664 --> 00:05:00.821
- [Fixer] You know, of course,
the informers, and you know,

00:05:00.821 --> 00:05:03.881
these Industrial Area
Asian towns are controlled

00:05:03.881 --> 00:05:07.781
by internal security
forces, Al-Fazaa police.

00:05:07.781 --> 00:05:10.320
- So, it's not very smart for me

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:12.270
to go filming around in that area?

00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:13.537
- [Fixer] Yeah.

00:05:13.537 --> 00:05:18.180
- Okay, and I think that's why
we want to figure out a way.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:19.878
- [Fixer] Have you ever
been to Doha, I mean-

00:05:19.878 --> 00:05:20.711
- [Johnny] No.
- in Qatar?

00:05:20.711 --> 00:05:22.139
- It's my first time.

00:05:22.139 --> 00:05:23.280
(fixer clears throat)

00:05:23.280 --> 00:05:24.180
What do you think?

00:05:25.219 --> 00:05:27.259
(dramatic music)

00:05:27.259 --> 00:05:28.092
- Okay.

00:05:30.990 --> 00:05:35.990
This is not happening,
this is not happening.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:42.270
If we can't do the shots,
then this story doesn't work,

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:44.250
meaning I won't go to Doha.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:47.820
So, it's pretty important
for us to know soon

00:05:47.820 --> 00:05:50.220
if this is feasible or
if it's not feasible.

00:05:50.220 --> 00:05:52.392
Iz, can you-

00:05:52.392 --> 00:05:54.420
- [Fixer] Yeah, yeah, I
understand, I understand.

00:05:54.420 --> 00:05:55.680
- Well, it's really nice to meet you.

00:05:55.680 --> 00:05:57.090
Thank you so much for chatting.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:01.320
I can't safely go into
this Industrial Area.

00:06:01.320 --> 00:06:02.550
Like, it's now clear to me, like,

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.380
every fixer has just been like, "No."

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:05.310
This guy just said it point blank.

00:06:05.310 --> 00:06:07.050
He's like, "You're a
white dude with a camera.

00:06:07.050 --> 00:06:09.270
Like, this is not safe."

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:11.370
- It feels like, if you go,
you're just gonna, what,

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:15.390
get shots of shiny buildings
and not actually gain access.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:16.223
- Yeah.

00:06:16.223 --> 00:06:17.820
- Which I guess could be cool.

00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:18.653
- No.

00:06:18.653 --> 00:06:20.190
- I mean, there's an option here

00:06:20.190 --> 00:06:23.790
where you try to find someone

00:06:23.790 --> 00:06:25.590
that could go in.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:27.480
- And then, if we could
get, like, a camera person

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:29.400
in Nepal, or Bangladesh, or somewhere

00:06:29.400 --> 00:06:31.440
where workers have been and gone home,

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:34.950
we could totally tell this story.

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.690
The World Cup is literally
a few weeks away.

00:06:36.690 --> 00:06:37.830
I got some work to do.

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:41.307
The new plan, find someone
on the ground in Qatar

00:06:41.307 --> 00:06:42.140
who will go

00:06:42.140 --> 00:06:45.030
into the Industrial Area
(paper rustling)

00:06:45.030 --> 00:06:46.920
and tell me why the hell the government is

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:50.066
so afraid of me going in with my camera.

00:06:50.066 --> 00:06:52.312
(paper rustling)

00:06:52.312 --> 00:06:53.773
(mouse clicking)

00:06:53.773 --> 00:06:55.443
Okay (sighs).

00:06:55.443 --> 00:06:57.510
Okay, before we continue,

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.610
I need to tell you about something,

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:02.910
which is that today's video
is not sponsored by any brand.

00:07:02.910 --> 00:07:04.920
Sometimes we do really deep dives

00:07:04.920 --> 00:07:08.220
into complicated and sensitive topics.

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:11.100
It's hard to find a sponsor
when we make stories like this.

00:07:11.100 --> 00:07:12.000
I wanna tell you about a way

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.710
that you can support what we're doing.

00:07:13.710 --> 00:07:15.450
If you're not interested in
hearing this pitch from me,

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.560
that's totally fine.

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:17.430
So, I'm gonna put a little bar

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:18.600
down here on the bottom of the screen.

00:07:18.600 --> 00:07:21.030
For the rest of you that
are still here, thank you,

00:07:21.030 --> 00:07:23.310
and I wanna tell you about The Newsroom.

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:25.680
The Newsroom is our community on Patreon,

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.450
which is more and more
turning into a place

00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:29.820
that I am very excited about.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:32.550
Journalism is changing,
and I'm making big bets

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:34.890
that the type of journalism
that will succeed

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.720
in the future is the type of journalism

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.360
that dives deep without the need

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:42.000
for a journalistic institution to dictate

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.530
what direction we need to go.

00:07:43.530 --> 00:07:46.920
I want the story to guide
me whatever way it takes me.

00:07:46.920 --> 00:07:48.000
And I'm allowed to do that

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.070
because I'm here on
YouTube with all of you.

00:07:50.070 --> 00:07:52.590
But doing this form of
journalism on YouTube is

00:07:52.590 --> 00:07:54.630
incredibly resource intensive.

00:07:54.630 --> 00:07:56.880
Behind the scenes, we have
a lot of people making sure

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:58.050
that we're factually accurate,

00:07:58.050 --> 00:08:00.870
that we are actually finding
the best facts possible.

00:08:00.870 --> 00:08:02.460
It's hard and resource intensive,

00:08:02.460 --> 00:08:03.990
but I'm gonna keep doing it.

00:08:03.990 --> 00:08:05.430
That's where you all come in.

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:07.560
For those who are supporting
over at The Newsroom,

00:08:07.560 --> 00:08:10.050
you allow us to do this
kind of journalism.

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:11.250
But if that's not enough for you,

00:08:11.250 --> 00:08:13.290
we also have some really cool perks,

00:08:13.290 --> 00:08:15.540
including an extra video every month.

00:08:15.540 --> 00:08:17.070
We do a behind-the-scenes
video every month,

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.660
where we show you everything
that is happening,

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:21.600
all of the people, and
personalities, and processes

00:08:21.600 --> 00:08:23.490
that make this stuff happen.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.890
There are a lot of really
fun, talented people

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.300
making this work possible.

00:08:27.300 --> 00:08:29.250
You also get access to one
of my scripts every month,

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:32.610
and you get access to some
exclusive Tom Fox tracks.

00:08:32.610 --> 00:08:33.660
Tom is our composer.

00:08:33.660 --> 00:08:34.740
He makes amazing music.

00:08:34.740 --> 00:08:36.810
We will give you some of
that music, royalty free,

00:08:36.810 --> 00:08:38.580
for you to use however you'd like.

00:08:38.580 --> 00:08:39.930
And we'll ask the community to vote

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:41.880
on thumbnails, and
titles, and video ideas.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.030
And I really value having a
smaller version of this group

00:08:45.030 --> 00:08:47.100
here on YouTube but, like,
over on The Newsroom.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:49.590
If you're not able to
support, that's totally fine.

00:08:49.590 --> 00:08:51.150
I appreciate you being
here in the first place.

00:08:51.150 --> 00:08:53.310
At the end of the day, being
here, watching the videos,

00:08:53.310 --> 00:08:56.370
sharing them is a huge way
that this community allows me

00:08:56.370 --> 00:08:58.860
to do what I can do to
make better journalism.

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:00.870
So, that's my little pitch to you

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.240
for those interested
and willing to support.

00:09:03.240 --> 00:09:05.250
I want to get back into this story

00:09:05.250 --> 00:09:08.195
and show you how we ended
up in this situation.

00:09:08.195 --> 00:09:11.280
(resolute music)

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.610
Qatar is a tiny, super-rich
country in the desert,

00:09:14.610 --> 00:09:18.116
and it sits on the largest known
natural gas field on Earth.

00:09:18.116 --> 00:09:18.949
(liquid sloshing)

00:09:18.949 --> 00:09:20.130
Since their independence in 1970,

00:09:20.130 --> 00:09:22.650
Qatar got really rich, really fast,

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:25.290
leapfrogging the normal
economic development process

00:09:25.290 --> 00:09:27.120
that countries go through as they grow.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.770
Usually, as a country gets rich,

00:09:28.770 --> 00:09:31.590
immigrants from poorer
neighboring countries migrate

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:33.360
in to take lower paying jobs
(machines buzzing)

00:09:33.360 --> 00:09:35.490
required to keep the economy growing,

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:36.900
construction, hospitality,

00:09:36.900 --> 00:09:39.360
manual labor, care-taking, food services,

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:40.200
you know what I mean.

00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:42.360
Every rich country experiences this,

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.230
but in Qatar,
(inquisitive music)

00:09:43.230 --> 00:09:45.030
all of their neighbors were also getting

00:09:45.030 --> 00:09:47.580
super rich super fast,
so they started looking

00:09:47.580 --> 00:09:50.040
elsewhere for cheap
labor, and soon, there was

00:09:50.040 --> 00:09:52.140
a flow of people taking these jobs.

00:09:52.140 --> 00:09:53.640
But there's a tension here.

00:09:53.640 --> 00:09:56.190
Thanks to all this
abundant oil and gas money,

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:59.310
the Qatari government provides
a luxurious welfare state

00:09:59.310 --> 00:10:02.100
to their citizens, free
healthcare, education,

00:10:02.100 --> 00:10:04.620
guaranteed jobs, subsidized housing,

00:10:04.620 --> 00:10:07.830
and literally, they just get
paychecks for being Qatari,

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:09.810
for winning the fossil-fuel jackpot.

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:12.090
So, Qatar needed labor
from other countries,

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:13.770
but they didn't wanna let these immigrants

00:10:13.770 --> 00:10:16.590
in on the sumptuous benefits
of their welfare state.

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.270
So, they started using this system,

00:10:18.270 --> 00:10:20.430
where employers could sponsor workers

00:10:20.430 --> 00:10:22.140
to come to Qatar to work.

00:10:22.140 --> 00:10:24.330
They wouldn't be citizens
or anything close to it.

00:10:24.330 --> 00:10:26.670
They would be totally at
the mercy of their employer.

00:10:26.670 --> 00:10:28.620
This was called the kafala system,

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:29.940
and it was the foundation

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:32.374
upon which Qatar built its country.

00:10:32.374 --> 00:10:36.207
(inquisitive music continues)

