- [Raj] 50 minutes into the ride,

00:20:20.190 --> 00:20:21.720
and we're kind of starting to see

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:24.483
these kind of accommodations
where the workers live.

00:20:30.930 --> 00:20:33.240
This is one of those
buses that the workers

00:20:33.240 --> 00:20:35.603
that live in the Industrial
Area use to commute.

00:20:37.680 --> 00:20:39.547
Today is Friday, and it's a leisure day

00:20:39.547 --> 00:20:43.590
for a lot of workers, as
you can see a lot of clothes

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:46.743
that have been washed and
left in the sun to be dried.

00:20:47.667 --> 00:20:49.500
- So, this is the Industrial Area.

00:20:49.500 --> 00:20:51.060
It's the thing I've been thinking

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:52.530
about for a very long time,

00:20:52.530 --> 00:20:55.020
and I'm finally seeing
the footage from inside,

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:58.650
and I have to say, it's not
anything super surprising.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.360
This is kind of anti-climatic in the sense

00:21:00.360 --> 00:21:03.390
that I'm just looking
at like a kind of dusty,

00:21:03.390 --> 00:21:06.150
dilapidated part of town
with a bunch of buildings

00:21:06.150 --> 00:21:08.790
that look the same, and
yet, I now know a lot more

00:21:08.790 --> 00:21:11.130
about what this place represents.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:12.240
Look at this.

00:21:12.240 --> 00:21:14.220
The Industrial Area isn't just far away.

00:21:14.220 --> 00:21:15.660
It's completely cut off.

00:21:15.660 --> 00:21:17.490
Here's the metro system, brand new,

00:21:17.490 --> 00:21:19.447
that they were planning to
build for the World Cup.

00:21:19.447 --> 00:21:21.090
This is a whole system,

00:21:21.090 --> 00:21:23.820
connects all of the stadiums and the city.

00:21:23.820 --> 00:21:27.450
You can see that they planned
a couple of these lines

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:29.460
to go out to the Industrial Area.

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:32.250
This would connect the
Industrial Area to the city,

00:21:32.250 --> 00:21:35.580
and yet, these (laughing)
lines aren't actually built.

00:21:35.580 --> 00:21:37.020
They're gonna start on these

00:21:37.020 --> 00:21:39.450
right after the World Cup is over.

00:21:39.450 --> 00:21:43.200
So, yeah, this place is just,
like, completely disconnected.

00:21:43.200 --> 00:21:44.460
I think I now see that,

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:47.730
and it's not just
disconnected unintentionally.

00:21:47.730 --> 00:21:50.700
This is very systematically,
intentionally disconnected

00:21:50.700 --> 00:21:52.020
from the rest of the city.

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:55.020
Our interviews in Nepal
gave us some clarity

00:21:55.020 --> 00:21:57.966
on what it's like to live out there.

00:21:57.966 --> 00:21:58.799
(mouse clicking)

00:21:58.799 --> 00:22:03.299
(Sushil speaking in foreign language)

00:22:05.837 --> 00:22:10.337
(Sushil speaking in foreign language)

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:14.400
- The next phase of the
Qatar trap has to do

00:22:14.400 --> 00:22:16.320
with how these people were exploited,

00:22:16.320 --> 00:22:18.510
how their rights were taken away from them

00:22:18.510 --> 00:22:20.518
to force them to work.

00:22:20.518 --> 00:22:23.070
(pensive music)

00:22:23.070 --> 00:22:25.860
To build the World Cup,
these workers were forced

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:28.320
to work in very horrible conditions.

00:22:28.320 --> 00:22:30.810
Look at the temperatures
in Doha in the summer,

00:22:30.810 --> 00:22:33.210
getting close to 50 degrees Celsius,

00:22:33.210 --> 00:22:34.980
close to 120 degrees Fahrenheit.

00:22:34.980 --> 00:22:38.400
They literally have
air-conditioned outdoor spaces.

00:22:38.400 --> 00:22:41.880
Look at that, air conditioning
outside on wheels.

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:44.190
The stadiums themselves
will have air conditioning.

00:22:44.190 --> 00:22:45.870
And yet, these workers are out there

00:22:45.870 --> 00:22:48.714
doing, like, manual labor in this heat.

00:22:48.714 --> 00:22:53.214
(Bikram speaking in foreign language)

00:22:57.990 --> 00:23:01.350
- A lot of workers report
being treated like animals,

00:23:01.350 --> 00:23:06.350
being yelled at and bossed
around in totally inhumane ways.

00:23:06.615 --> 00:23:11.198
(Bikram speaking in foreign language)

00:23:17.610 --> 00:23:19.410
- Behind these walls, the conditions

00:23:19.410 --> 00:23:21.180
that these people were made to live in

00:23:21.180 --> 00:23:22.500
and really given no choice

00:23:22.500 --> 00:23:25.374
on where they could live are horrendous.

00:23:25.374 --> 00:23:29.874
(Bikram speaking in foreign language)

00:23:31.858 --> 00:23:36.441
(Sushil speaking in foreign language)

00:23:40.200 --> 00:23:41.910
- Journalists and human
rights organizations have

00:23:41.910 --> 00:23:44.250
actually gotten cameras
back here to actually show

00:23:44.250 --> 00:23:45.180
what that looks like.

00:23:45.180 --> 00:23:48.120
The heat and conditions
got so bad for some workers

00:23:48.120 --> 00:23:49.920
that they never returned home.

00:23:51.598 --> 00:23:55.931
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:23:58.092 --> 00:24:00.934
(dramatic music)

00:24:00.934 --> 00:24:05.267
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:24:06.944 --> 00:24:11.277
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:24:16.418 --> 00:24:20.751
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:24:25.894 --> 00:24:26.727
(camera clicking)

00:24:26.727 --> 00:24:31.144
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:24:34.860 --> 00:24:38.940
- Thousands of totally
healthy young men died

00:24:38.940 --> 00:24:41.183
while working in these conditions.

00:24:41.183 --> 00:24:42.016
(inquisitive music)

00:24:42.016 --> 00:24:43.380
We'll likely never know
the true cause of death

00:24:43.380 --> 00:24:45.030
because instead of a real investigation,

00:24:45.030 --> 00:24:47.430
the Qatari authorities come out and use

00:24:47.430 --> 00:24:50.640
these vague classifications
like heart failure

00:24:50.640 --> 00:24:53.490
and natural causes as the cause of death.

00:24:53.490 --> 00:24:56.310
Doing this robs the family of answers

00:24:56.310 --> 00:24:59.943
on why their loved one came home in a box.

00:25:01.709 --> 00:25:04.671
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:25:04.671 --> 00:25:07.254
(gentle music)

00:25:10.740 --> 00:25:12.510
- So, if these employers are so bad,

00:25:12.510 --> 00:25:15.030
why don't these employees
just change jobs?

00:25:15.030 --> 00:25:16.550
The answer is they can't.

00:25:16.550 --> 00:25:17.580
(pensive music)
For a long time, legally,

00:25:17.580 --> 00:25:19.440
they couldn't because the next part

00:25:19.440 --> 00:25:22.567
of this trap has to do with paperwork.

00:25:22.567 --> 00:25:27.067
(Sushil speaking in foreign language)

00:25:31.015 --> 00:25:35.040
(Sushil speaking in foreign language)

00:25:35.040 --> 00:25:37.080
- Oftentimes this
paperwork would stipulate

00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:39.450
that these workers can't change jobs

00:25:39.450 --> 00:25:41.250
without the permission of their employers.

00:25:41.250 --> 00:25:43.470
So, the status of these
workers who were trapped

00:25:43.470 --> 00:25:47.400
in their little blue box on
the outskirts of the city was

00:25:47.400 --> 00:25:50.100
completely at the mercy
of their employers.

00:25:50.100 --> 00:25:53.190
If they left their job,
they would be considered

00:25:53.190 --> 00:25:55.800
a foreign immigrant illegally there

00:25:55.800 --> 00:25:57.721
and could be arrested and put into jail.

00:25:57.721 --> 00:26:01.200
(Sushil speaking in foreign language)

00:26:01.200 --> 00:26:03.090
- Just one more layer of the trap.

00:26:03.090 --> 00:26:03.923
And then, there was the fact

00:26:03.923 --> 00:26:06.870
that these employers would
often not pay their workers

00:26:06.870 --> 00:26:09.690
for months at a time
withholding wages from them

00:26:09.690 --> 00:26:12.450
and thus increasing their
leverage and power over them.

00:26:12.450 --> 00:26:13.620
And with no recourse,

00:26:13.620 --> 00:26:15.480
these workers couldn't
do anything about it.

00:26:15.480 --> 00:26:16.980
So, yes, we are now talking

00:26:16.980 --> 00:26:20.820
about forced labor with no compensation,

00:26:20.820 --> 00:26:23.640
a euphemism for modern-day slavery.

00:26:23.640 --> 00:26:24.690
I know that sounds dramatic,

00:26:24.690 --> 00:26:26.490
but that's literally
what is happening here,

00:26:26.490 --> 00:26:27.660
not to all workers.

00:26:27.660 --> 00:26:29.063
There were workers who
had great conditions

00:26:29.063 --> 00:26:30.660
and who got paid on time,

00:26:30.660 --> 00:26:34.770
but this system enabled firms
to so deeply exploit workers

00:26:34.770 --> 00:26:37.230
because it gave them
so much power over them

00:26:37.230 --> 00:26:39.630
and so little recourse for these workers

00:26:39.630 --> 00:26:40.770
to complain or do anything

00:26:40.770 --> 00:26:42.570
without being punished or arrested.

00:26:42.570 --> 00:26:44.070
So, with with no other options,

00:26:44.070 --> 00:26:47.261
some workers turned to their
last resort, protesting.

00:26:47.261 --> 00:26:48.198
(dramatic music)

00:26:48.198 --> 00:26:50.047
(protestors speaking in foreign language)

00:26:50.047 --> 00:26:54.547
(Sushil speaking in foreign language)

00:26:57.682 --> 00:27:01.289
(Sushil speaking in foreign language)

00:27:01.289 --> 00:27:05.580
(protestors speaking in foreign language)

00:27:05.580 --> 00:27:09.497
- Here they are blocking
traffic, central Doha.

00:27:11.861 --> 00:27:13.020
(mouse clicking)

00:27:13.020 --> 00:27:14.370
But don't be fooled here.

00:27:14.370 --> 00:27:16.560
This wasn't some worker uprising.

00:27:16.560 --> 00:27:18.690
This type of thing is illegal in Qatar,

00:27:18.690 --> 00:27:20.160
an authoritarian police state

00:27:20.160 --> 00:27:23.400
where assembly like this
is totally not okay.

00:27:23.400 --> 00:27:25.500
So, what happened is the
police would show up,

00:27:25.500 --> 00:27:27.240
squash these protests, tell them

00:27:27.240 --> 00:27:28.260
that everything was gonna be okay

00:27:28.260 --> 00:27:30.420
and they would get paid and then deported

00:27:30.420 --> 00:27:32.880
a huge number of these people,
got them outta the system

00:27:32.880 --> 00:27:35.070
so that the status quo could remain.

00:27:35.070 --> 00:27:37.140
- [Raj] Just dehumanizing
people that belong

00:27:37.140 --> 00:27:41.010
to a certain race and are brought here

00:27:41.010 --> 00:27:44.250
for certain purposes is
not justified by any means.

00:27:44.250 --> 00:27:45.780
- Thanks to international scrutiny,

00:27:45.780 --> 00:27:48.000
Qatar started to make some reforms.

00:27:48.000 --> 00:27:49.290
They realized this wasn't gonna fly

00:27:49.290 --> 00:27:50.610
if they were gonna host the World Cup.

00:27:50.610 --> 00:27:53.850
So, they started instituting
things like worker hours

00:27:53.850 --> 00:27:55.560
that were not in the heat of the day,

00:27:55.560 --> 00:27:58.860
mandatory water on site so these
people could stay hydrated,

00:27:58.860 --> 00:28:00.810
a minimum wage, changing the law

00:28:00.810 --> 00:28:03.870
so that people could
technically change jobs

00:28:03.870 --> 00:28:06.300
without permission, compensating families

00:28:06.300 --> 00:28:07.950
for people who died working.

00:28:07.950 --> 00:28:09.660
All of this looked great on paper,

00:28:09.660 --> 00:28:11.460
but human rights organizations

00:28:11.460 --> 00:28:13.890
like Amnesty International
actually have looked to see

00:28:13.890 --> 00:28:17.400
if those policies have
trickled into reality.

00:28:17.400 --> 00:28:19.170
And you know what I'm gonna say.

00:28:19.170 --> 00:28:20.138
They haven't.

00:28:20.138 --> 00:28:21.984
(pensive music)

00:28:21.984 --> 00:28:24.141
- [Raj] This is the Shahaniya labor camp.

00:28:24.141 --> 00:28:25.713
This is big walls.

00:28:27.063 --> 00:28:30.010
A lot of people live here as well.

00:28:30.010 --> 00:28:33.510
(pensive music continues)

00:28:35.550 --> 00:28:37.980
- So, yeah, I really understand now

00:28:37.980 --> 00:28:41.940
what this little blue box
is for, what it represents.

00:28:41.940 --> 00:28:43.740
The authorities in Doha are getting ready

00:28:43.740 --> 00:28:46.560
for this World Cup, and
as the event approaches,

00:28:46.560 --> 00:28:48.990
they are making sure
that anyone who belongs

00:28:48.990 --> 00:28:52.239
in this box stays in that box.

00:28:52.239 --> 00:28:54.000
(dramatic music)
Okay, this is insane,

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:55.110
the timing of this.

00:28:55.110 --> 00:28:56.670
This is literally happening right now.

00:28:56.670 --> 00:28:59.430
- [Raj] The whole thing
has just been wiped out

00:29:00.380 --> 00:29:03.000
by some weird phenomenon.

00:29:03.000 --> 00:29:05.160
- I just got a message from Raj

00:29:05.160 --> 00:29:09.600
that they are evicting
workers from the city.

00:29:09.600 --> 00:29:12.150
People who are living
(paper rustling)

00:29:12.150 --> 00:29:13.860
in the yellow area illegally

00:29:13.860 --> 00:29:16.110
because of the law are being evicted.

00:29:16.110 --> 00:29:17.940
It's a couple weeks before the World Cup,

00:29:17.940 --> 00:29:20.460
and so the timing is not surprising

00:29:20.460 --> 00:29:22.116
that they are cracking down.

00:29:22.116 --> 00:29:23.280
(paper rustling)

00:29:23.280 --> 00:29:24.530
- [Raj] Locks everywhere,

00:29:26.280 --> 00:29:28.380
everything looks like it
has been done really quick.

00:29:28.380 --> 00:29:30.090
They are literally catching people

00:29:30.090 --> 00:29:32.126
and putting them into Shahaniya,

00:29:32.126 --> 00:29:33.330
which is the Industrial Area.

00:29:33.330 --> 00:29:36.390
I'm trying to get footages
of them being evicted

00:29:36.390 --> 00:29:38.550
because a lot of them are being evicted,

00:29:38.550 --> 00:29:41.070
like, just with two hours of notice.

00:29:41.070 --> 00:29:42.570
That's what I'm trying to do now.

00:29:42.570 --> 00:29:45.120
- This is so clear to me what's happening.

00:29:45.120 --> 00:29:48.360
They're clearly starting to really enforce

00:29:48.360 --> 00:29:50.820
this, like, family zoning
thing to get anyone

00:29:50.820 --> 00:29:53.460
who they don't want to be seen

00:29:53.460 --> 00:29:56.670
out of the center of the city.

00:29:56.670 --> 00:29:58.590
I've never done a story
(laughs) like this before.

00:29:58.590 --> 00:30:01.410
This is developing, like, day by day,

00:30:01.410 --> 00:30:04.440
and all of this reporting that we've done,

00:30:04.440 --> 00:30:07.260
I'm now seeing it play out in real time

00:30:07.260 --> 00:30:09.150
as the city prepares for the World Cup,

00:30:09.150 --> 00:30:13.020
using all of these laws to
continue to hide these people,

00:30:13.020 --> 00:30:14.190
to get them out of view

00:30:14.190 --> 00:30:17.228
as all of these international
visitors prepare to come.

00:30:17.228 --> 00:30:20.065
- [Raj] It feels so empty,
and it's only the small houses

00:30:20.065 --> 00:30:21.513
that have been evacuated.

00:30:21.513 --> 00:30:23.247
(inquisitive music)

00:30:23.247 --> 00:30:26.497
- [Announcer] Strike, against the post.

00:30:31.348 --> 00:30:33.716
(papers rustling)

00:30:33.716 --> 00:30:36.226
(mouse clicking)

00:30:36.226 --> 00:30:40.510
- Okay, well we got to the bottom of it.

00:30:40.510 --> 00:30:41.343
(papers rustling)

00:30:41.343 --> 00:30:45.900
We know what know why this
exists, the way it's drawn,

00:30:45.900 --> 00:30:47.850
what it means,
(papers thudding)

00:30:47.850 --> 00:30:49.472
who it's for, what it's meant to do.

00:30:49.472 --> 00:30:51.360
(headset thudding)

00:30:51.360 --> 00:30:53.190
I did not expect that.

00:30:53.190 --> 00:30:55.230
I know what's happening
behind those walls,

00:30:55.230 --> 00:30:59.190
how those people are trapped,
how their families miss them,

00:30:59.190 --> 00:31:02.362
and how some of them
might never come home.

00:31:02.362 --> 00:31:06.695
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:31:08.957 --> 00:31:13.687
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:31:13.687 --> 00:31:18.020
(Goma speaking in foreign language)

00:31:22.860 --> 00:31:24.660
- Now, let's be clear, this happened

00:31:24.660 --> 00:31:27.120
well before the World
Cup ever came to Qatar.

00:31:27.120 --> 00:31:30.240
And what I fear is that,
once we all move on,

00:31:30.240 --> 00:31:33.120
once these few weeks of
playing football are over,

00:31:33.120 --> 00:31:34.890
we'll forget about everything we saw,

00:31:34.890 --> 00:31:36.270
and Qatar will have no incentive

00:31:36.270 --> 00:31:38.760
to actually do anything about this.

00:31:38.760 --> 00:31:41.430
And they'll go back to what
they've been doing for decades,

00:31:41.430 --> 00:31:44.820
deceiving these workers,
trapping them in their country,

00:31:44.820 --> 00:31:48.088
exploiting them, and then
hiding them from view.

00:31:48.088 --> 00:31:50.230
(papers rustling)

00:31:50.230 --> 00:31:53.230
(inquisitive music)

00:32:09.743 --> 00:32:13.576
(inquisitive music continues)

